---
title: dinyd · check verdicts
config:
  look: handDrawn
  handDrawnSeed: 5
  theme: dark
  themeVariables:
    mainBkg: "#333333"
    clusterBkg: "#242424"
  themeCSS: |
    small { display: inline-block; text-align: left; }
  flowchart:
    wrappingWidth: 300
---
%% Behavior authority: this diagram and anchors.mermaid.
%% Basis: --index (default · for gates) · --worktree (for checking while working) · --rev commit. Documents and targets are read from the same basis. --index and --rev read through the Git CLI (ls-files --stage -z · ls-tree -r -z --full-tree · cat-file --batch) and honor GIT_INDEX_FILE. --worktree reads the disk.
%% Scope: all (default · for gates) · --changed [--base rev]. --changed selects only anchors in changed documents and anchors whose target path changed (deletions · renames included). Without --base it compares against HEAD; with --rev, --base is required. Malformed anchors are always included.
%% Invalid: a malformed anchor (malformed); a target that is missing · matches two or more · is a disallowed entry (symlink · gitlink · intent-to-add under --index · unmerged under --index · --worktree) · fails to parse (unresolved). dinyd-ref also accepts a directory as its target.
%% The digest is recomputed with the mode recorded in the anchor (s1 · b1).
%% Failure output is one line per anchor (document path → selector: verdict + next step), with no line numbers or document content. Usage and read errors exit 2 with a message on stderr.
flowchart LR
  Collect["collect anchors<br/><small>• read documents · targets from the basis<br/>• all or --changed</small>"]
  Found{"are the reference and target valid?"}
  Digest{"digest"}
  Ok["ok"]

  subgraph Fail["exit 1 · the document must be opened"]
    Broken["malformed · unresolved<br/><small>re-judge the claim and the reference</small>"]
    Undeclared["undeclared<br/><small>fill the digest with update</small>"]
    Stale["stale<br/><small>re-judge the claim, then update</small>"]
  end

  Collect --> Found
  Found -->|no| Broken
  Found -->|yes · dinyd-ref| Ok
  Found -->|yes · dinyd| Digest
  Digest -->|none| Undeclared
  Digest -->|differs| Stale
  Digest -->|equal| Ok

  classDef em fill:#173d25,stroke:#86efac
  class Fail em
